acceptance_criteria: "Every command declares its exit-code set in the same contract tables that already carry its flags and error codes, and the set is rendered by the contracts output; The vocabulary distinguishes succeeded with effect, succeeded with no effect, refused for input, refused for tracker state, and internal failure; A conformance check asserts no command returns an undeclared code and every declared code is reachable from the replay corpus, with a negative control; The scripting contract documents the exit-code semantics once, and no command describes its own numeric convention separately"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: 82
resolution: Implemented generated SDK and CLI exit-effect contracts with stable success exits 6 and 7 and replay conformance.
expected_result: Every active core command has a generated numeric exit set; contracts output exposes the vocabulary; real bulk mutations distinguish full no and partial effect; conformance fails on undeclared or unreachable exits.
actual_result: All core roots are generated from PM_CORE_COMMAND_NAMES; full contracts output groups equivalent sets token-efficiently; update-many and close-many emit 0 effect 6 no_effect and 7 partial_effect; telemetry treats all three as success; real temporary-tracker replay and negative controls pass.
